---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---
<PageLayout title="Pose Detection — Alex Sheen">
  <div class="base_padding">
    <div class="w3-row">
      <div class="projtitle white_text base_padding" style="width:100%">
        Pose-Detection
        <div class="projtext" style="width:100%">
          <br />
          <div class="vl">
            TensorFlow<br />
            2022<br />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="proj" style="width:100%">
        <video style="width:100%" muted autoplay loop playsinline>
          <source src="/assets/videos/pose-detection/posenet.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          Your browser does not support the video tag.
        </video>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="w3-row">
      <div class="w3-half base_padding">
        <div class="proj" style="width:100%">
          <div class="projtitle white_text" style="width:100%">
            <div class="projtext" style="width:100%">
              This project used pre-trained pose-detection TensorFlow.js models to create an interactive art installation which was
              showcased in the lobby of UChicago's Media Arts, Data, and Design Center (MADD).<br /><br />

              I set up a camera to catch the movements of passersby
              and projected the generated visual on to the wall using the MADD center's projector. Various parameters are tied to the position, distance, angle,
              and speed of the user's hands, feet, and arms. The installation accommodated multiple users.

              <br /><br />
              Unfortunately, I can't find videos/images of the installation at the moment, but you can see a test-run of the pose-detection to the right.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="w3-half base_padding">
        <div class="proj" style="width:100%">
          <video style="width:100%" muted autoplay loop playsinline>
            <source src="/assets/videos/pose-detection/blazepose.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
            Your browser does not support the video tag.
          </video>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
